hink about it because it  looks natural but if you go frame by  frame you can see her feet bounce in a  particular way and her body position  changed depending on what kind of  platform she's running on number four  not the class science project you're  used to in this high-powered finale  there are major moments that rely  heavily on the VFX team when our heroes  head back to high school to set some  major Home Alone style traps they fill  the school with what's known as elephant  toothpaste this gray CG foam-like  substance was created by the VFX team  and it's only animated as it expands  throughout the building they actually  spent more time on this 12 second shot  than anything else in the whole show  number five also known as the most  efficient form of transportation  creating kamala's hard light platforms  were pertinent to the VFX team there's  an important scene where she is training  on a rooftop jumping from platform to  platform the sequence utilizes clean  almost virtually clear plates and  digitally generated backgrounds to give  the impression that she is in fact  running through the city rise VFX  supervisor Stuart Bowlen shares one of  the major challenges of perfecting these  platforms there's a narrow window where  the hard light needed to look solid with  a fine balance of opacity versus  opaqueness while avoiding looking like  Crystal so the development of the powers  went through many subtle adjustments  until we settled on the right balance  number six there were at least three  Digi doubles for Kamala the artistic use  of Digi doubles was an important factor  in making sure they could showcase  kamala's powers and the Damage Done to  the city in a realistic Way by working  with full body scans of Iman villani  they were able to create a full body  duplicate of her and several other  characters and place them in dangerous  situations without worry they were also  able to edit the live-action footage and  remove any imperfections that would take  away from the scene Stuart Bowlen shares  with awn what it was like to choreograph  these scenes at times we needed Kamala  to land on the hard light platforms  where they absorbed her kinetic energy  so we relied upon swapping out Iman  villani for our Digi double to allow for  a more natural reaction between the two  number seven some sick visuals here an  important task for the rise VFX team was  being able to show a smooth transition  between the nor Dimension Karachi and  then Earth we settled on glass panes  that rise out of the floor and in  between these panes sand Rises up to  form those worlds this was the first  time that the nor Dimension has been  visually represented in any way in the  Marvel Cinematic Universe and so it was  our task to imagine how that should look  Stuart Bowlen describes it as an fx  supervisor's dream number eight more  like the breakable CGI panel most shows  would typically use breakable glass when  it came to bursting through a door but  as you can see the visual effects were  so smoothly done you wouldn't even know  it was CGI unless disclosed Farhan  akhtar's character Walid is shown  bursting through a door at Red dagger's  headquarters and as shown by Rise that  glass panel was completely generated by  the VFX team to ensure a smooth take  number nine a must have for any MCU  battle a major part of depicting the  fight scenes in Miss Marvel were the  utilization of CG weapons Iman villani  and her co-stars would depict the  movements separately and then get  rendered into a digidouble so they could  then place them into a realistically  dangerous fight sequence without needing  an actual prop in place Dort Bullen  explains the fight scenes on set were  carefully choreographed and so how the  hard light platforms move around to the  scenes and are also used as Weapons was  choreographed at rise number 10 let's  get into kamala's iconic MCU Powers we  talked a little bit about how they were  able to depict the Larger than 