d in the  Islamic Institute of Atlanta for all of  their digital references number 14  working with light bulbs on camera is an  art form when creating kamala's powers  on screen one of the biggest challenges  was getting the lighting just right the  cinematographer Jules O'Loughlin wanted  to do as much as possible on camera so  they didn't have to leave everything to  the VFX team it's a real dance between  getting lighting fixtures on the set but  hiding them from the camera I used  larger than lighting fixtures off camera  for energy walls and the light and then  smaller LEDs behind her arms or in her  clothes hiding smaller units around the  set number 15 we're here for every panel  one thing the LOL follow really wanted  to do when it came to Bringing Miss  Marvel to life was utilize a comic book  style animation when showing what it was  like to be inside kamala's head he talks  to slash film about the inspiration  behind that we were a bit afraid that  Marvel wouldn't do that because it's  totally different than all of the other  shows so we really tried to present this  presentation to Kevin feige to show that  with animation we can go inside her head  her Fantasyland and Her Imagination  without this aesthetic they would have  been Limited in kamala's  characterization after learning all the  visual effects secrets from digital  domain and Rise we're even more  impressed with Miss Marvel's hard light  Powers the beautiful set of New Jersey  and the seamless incorporation of  Animation to create this modern MCU  Universe what was your favorite moment  in the series
 

